{
  "format": "kshader",
  "generator": "Kekenik Shader",
  "graph": {
    "comments": [
      {
        "color": "#60a5fa",
        "id": "note_geo",
        "position": {
          "x": 22,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 56,
          "w": 762
        },
        "text": "Object-space position drives the flake cells; world normal, view and the *Light Direction* parameter decide when a flake reflects light into the camera. Shared through portals."
      },
      {
        "color": "#4ade80",
        "id": "note_bump",
        "position": {
          "x": 988,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 56,
          "w": 1460
        },
        "text": "Two octaves of cheap value-fbm are the height; **Height To Normal** (fast kernel) turns it into a tangent-space normal for the Lit master. The same height tints dips with the shade colour and darkens crevices (occlusion)."
      },
      {
        "color": "#22d3ee",
        "id": "note_flake",
        "position": {
          "x": 988,
          "y": 910
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 2990
        },
        "text": "Object position × density is split into an integer **cell** and a fractional position inside it. One hash of the cell gives a random vector: it jitters the flake centre (±¼ of the cell) and tilts the flake normal `normalize(N + d × tilt)`. A radial mask keeps a small disc per cell."
      },
      {
        "color": "#fbbf24",
        "id": "note_glint",
        "position": {
          "x": 4182,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 2684
        },
        "text": "Half vector `H = normalize(L + V)`; a flake glints when its normal lines up with H: `pow(saturate(F·H), sharpness)`. Multiplied by the disc mask, the sun-facing term and a per-flake twinkle `½ + ½·sin(t·3 + id·37)` (id = cell hash) blended by *Twinkle*."
      },
      {
        "color": "#fb923c",
        "id": "note_emit",
        "position": {
          "x": 7070,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 56,
          "w": 848
        },
        "text": "`emission = sparkleColor × glint × intensity` — emission is HDR, so strong glints bloom in the preview and in URP/Godot with Bloom enabled."
      },
      {
        "color": "#a78bfa",
        "id": "note_out",
        "position": {
          "x": 8122,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 56,
          "w": 542
        },
        "text": "Tangent-space bump normal, tinted albedo, crevice occlusion and glint emission."
      }
    ],
